# Top-level (direct) Python dependencies for the XC Data Platform.
#
# This is the human-edited source of truth. Do NOT pip-install from this file
# directly for reproducible environments — install from the fully pinned,
# hashed lockfile instead:
#
#     pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.lock
#
# Regenerate the lockfile after any change here (Requirement 16.7):
#
#     pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file requirements.lock requirements.in
#
# See docs/dependency-review.md for the review + rollback process.

# --- Current operational dashboard / pipeline (legacy, kept runnable) ---
streamlit==1.50.0
pandas==2.2.3
plotly==6.3.1
beautifulsoup4==4.14.2
lxml==6.0.2
numpy==2.3.4

# --- New platform development toolchain (Task 1.3) ---
# Formatter + linter, type checker, and test runner for src/xc_platform.
# Configured in pyproject.toml. These are exact pins per Requirement 16.7.
ruff==0.11.9
mypy==1.14.1
pytest==8.3.0
pytest-cov==6.0.0

# --- AWS SDK (Task 6) ---
# S3 snapshot publication/reader client (design.md section 7). Reviewed per
# docs/dependency-review.md section 3 and escalated per its "AWS SDK bringing
# its own network client" clause -- AWS's official SDK, maintained by AWS,
# no install-time scripts, license Apache-2.0. Transitive deps (botocore,
# s3transfer, urllib3, jmespath, python-dateutil) are all part of the same
# AWS SDK family or already-standard HTTP/date libraries.
boto3==1.43.99

# --- Strands Agents SDK (Task 11.3-11.5) ---
# Runtime-neutral agent framework: the same Agent/tool definitions run
# locally (dev/test, no AWS calls) and under AgentCore Runtime (Task
# 11.5). Escalated per docs/dependency-review.md section 3's "agent SDK
# bringing its own network client" clause -- owner-authorized 2026-09-22
# in-session for this task. AWS-authored (Amazon/AWS org), Apache-2.0,
# "Production/Stable" classifier, actively released (1.56.0 as of this
# pin). Installed with no extras: this project only needs the core
# Agent/tool/BedrockModel surface the Task 3.5 feasibility prototype
# (feasibility/agent/agent_core.py) already validated, not the
# `[all]` extra's litellm/anthropic/google-genai/a2a bundle. Core
# transitive deps are boto3/botocore (already a reviewed dependency),
# docstring-parser, httpx, jsonschema, mcp, opentelemetry-api/sdk/
# instrumentation-threading, pydantic, pyyaml, typing-extensions,
# watchdog -- all mainstream, no install-time scripts.
strands-agents==1.56.0

# --- Bedrock AgentCore SDK (Task 11.5) ---
# The `@app.entrypoint`/BedrockAgentCoreApp runtime contract the Task 3.5
# feasibility prototype validated live (docs/agentcore-deployment-evidence.md)
# and this task's production entrypoint modules
# (src/xc_platform/agents/agentcore_entrypoints/) implement for real, without
# deploying anything (owner decision, 2026-09-22 in-session for this task).
# Escalated per docs/dependency-review.md section 3's "agent SDK bringing its
# own network client" clause -- same authorization as strands-agents above.
# AWS-authored (Amazon/AWS org), Apache-2.0. Classifier is "Development
# Status: 3 - Alpha" (less mature than strands-agents' "Production/Stable"),
# consistent with the feasibility evidence's own finding that this SDK/CLI
# surface has real rough edges (docs/agentcore-deployment-evidence.md's
# actor-isolation gap, the Python starter-toolkit deprecation noted in
# feasibility/agentcore/README.md) -- tracked as a known risk, not a reason
# to avoid the only supported AgentCore Runtime integration path. Installed
# with no extras (a2a/ag-ui/autoevals are unused). Core transitive deps are
# boto3/botocore (already reviewed), pydantic (already a strands-agents
# transitive dependency), starlette/uvicorn/websockets (the entrypoint's HTTP
# server), typing-extensions, urllib3 -- all mainstream, no install-time
# scripts.
bedrock-agentcore==1.23.1

# --- FastAPI web/API framework (Task 13) ---
# The versioned `/api/v1` REST + WebSocket surface (design.md section 13).
# Not an AWS/agent SDK, so no dependency-review escalation applies -- a
# mainstream, "Production/Stable"-tier web framework, Apache-licensed
# (MIT), no install-time scripts. `uvicorn` was already a transitive
# dependency of bedrock-agentcore; pinned directly here too since this
# project now imports/runs it directly (the ASGI server), not just via a
# transitive chain. Session/CSRF/connection-ticket signing uses stdlib
# `hmac`/`hashlib` rather than adding `itsdangerous` (stdlib-first,
# docs/dependency-review.md).
fastapi==0.141.1
uvicorn==0.53.0
